<style is:global>
  /*
   * ONE RULE, AND IT HAS TO BE GLOBAL.
   *
   * These preview badges are `<Badge>` components now, and an Astro SCOPED rule does not reach the
   * root element a child component renders — the repo has lost rules to exactly this twice, and both
   * gates stay green while the declaration quietly does nothing. The selector is already prefixed
   * with this view's own `.rpd-prev-row`, so global costs nothing in reach.
   *
   * What it does: keep the change/status badge on one line (e.g. "Formula changed") so the name
   * beside it ellipsises instead of the badge wrapping.
   */
  .rpd-prev-row .badge { flex: none; white-space: nowrap; }

  /* ── THE HISTORY TABLE'S OWN RULES, GLOBAL FOR THE SAME REASON AS THE BADGE ABOVE ──────────────
     `Table.astro` renders the `<thead>`, so every `<th>` carries the VESSEL's `data-astro-cid-…`
     and a scoped `.rpd-tablewrap :is(th, td)` matches the `td` half only — silently, with ds-lint,
     typecheck, css-guard and smoke all green. The `.rpd-` prefix is unique to this view, so
     `is:global` costs no reach.

     `auto`, NOT `clip` — the same S1 as the Reports list (`ReportsView.astro`), measured on this
     very table: at **1280, the app's own boundary**, 169px was hidden and `Delivery` was gone; at
     540, 483px and four of six facts including `Generated`, the column that says whether the run
     produced anything. `clip` is not a scroll container, so none of it could be reached by any
     means. `narrow="fold"` is the answer below 1280; `auto` covers the band above it. */
  .rpd-tablewrap { overflow-x: auto; }
  .rpd-tablewrap :is(th, td) { white-space: nowrap; }
</style>
